From 7da7edfabc6d4b44017f3fb60d0aa976d2535b4d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:39:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ST-005 follow-up: enable Save on Edit Total Due

Editing one player's Total Due inherited the bulk "Set dues for all
players" scope, so the Save button applied the bulk guard (disabled when
no rostered player is without dues). Once every player had dues, Save
could never enable. An edit is now always a single-player edit, and Save
reads one shared rule (canSaveDuesForm): enabled only when the amount is
a valid number that differs from the current Total Due.

A server rejection (e.g. Total Due below payments already recorded) is
now shown inside the open dues form instead of behind it.

Server-side protections unchanged: the payment floor in savePlayerPayment,
no payment_log writes on Total Due edits, the bulk Team Dues restrictions,
and Set Dues behaviour.

Adds scripts/check-dues-edit.js (44 behavioural assertions) to npm run check.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01U71QFs2ZMqAJL3URRe7Bix
